---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components

1) LiteRT-LM (Google LLC)
   Source / binary: https://github.com/google-ai-edge/LiteRT-LM
   License: Apache License 2.0
   Local checkout (developers): ios/.tools/LiteRT-LM after running
   ios/scripts/bootstrap-litertlm.sh — that tree includes its own LICENSE.
   The application links the LiteRTLM Swift package and CLiteRTLM xcframework
   from the pinned release tag documented in ios/docs/development.md.

2) Gemma model weights (Google)
   Not included in this repository. Users obtain `.litertlm` weights separately
   and import them on device.
   Terms: https://ai.google.dev/gemma/terms
   Docs: https://ai.google.dev/gemma

3) multilingual-e5-small (intfloat)
   Source: https://huggingface.co/intfloat/multilingual-e5-small
   License: MIT
   The release application redistributes a locally converted, INT8
   weight-quantized Core ML artifact and its tokenizer. It is used only for
   on-device document and query embeddings; the application never downloads
   this model at runtime.

4) huggingface/swift-transformers (Tokenizers)
   Source: https://github.com/huggingface/swift-transformers
   License: Apache License 2.0
   Used to load the bundled offline tokenizer for multilingual-e5-small.

5) Apple system frameworks (Vision, CoreML, PDFKit, Accelerate, SwiftUI, …)
   Used under Apple SDK license terms; not redistributed here.

6) ZIPFoundation (Thomas Zoechling / weichsel)
   Source: https://github.com/weichsel/ZIPFoundation
   License: MIT
   Used by Infrastructure to open Office Open XML packages (docx / xlsx /
   pptx) for on-device Markdown text extraction.

7) Material Icon Theme file icons (Material Extensions)
   Source: https://github.com/material-extensions/vscode-material-icon-theme
   License: MIT
   Bundled PNG derivatives (Word / Excel / PowerPoint / PDF / Markdown /
   plain text) under ios/Sources/Resources/Assets.xcassets/FileIcon*.imageset
   for the knowledge-base document list.
